          "hidden": true,
          "longAbout": null,
          "name": "hook",
          "owner": "python-quality",
          "path": [
            "python-quality",
            "hook"
          ],
          "placeholder": false
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "hidden": false,
      "longAbout": "python-quality has no verbs: its rules run after every edit of a .py file in a Python project (pyproject.toml, setup.py, setup.cfg or requirements.txt) with python3 on PATH. Violations (oversized files and functions, misplaced or misnamed tests, bare except, blanket # noqa or # type: ignore, mocks in tests) fail the file's quality-gate entry until it is fixed; a public def or class without a docstring is an advisory.\n\nLimits come from lang.python in toolu.config.json (maxFileLines, maxFnLines, noMocks). Run toolu doctor to see whether the rule is registered and compiled in.",
      "name": "python-quality",
      "owner": "python-quality",
      "path": [
        "python-quality"
      ],
      "placeholder": false
    },
    {
      "about": "Rust quality rules that run after each edit",
      "aliases": [],
      "args": [],
      "commands": [
        {
          "about": "Run the blocking Rust quality rules over a repository's .rs files",
          "aliases": [],
          "args": [
            {
              "help": "Directories or files to check, relative to the working directory",
              "multiple": true,
              "name": "PATH",
              "required": false
            }
          ],
          "commands": [],
          "flags": [],
          "hidden": false,
          "longAbout": "Run the blocking Rust quality rules over every tracked or untracked, not ignored .rs file under the paths (the whole repository by default), with the limits of lang.rust in toolu.config.json. Prints one block per finding. Exits 1 with findings or when git fails, 69 without ast-grep.",
          "name": "check",
          "owner": "rust-quality",
          "path": [
            "rust-quality",
            "check"
          ],
          "placeholder": false
        },
        {
          "about": "Run a hook entry; hooks.json calls it (internal)",
          "aliases": [],
          "args": [
            {
              "help": "The hook entry, as its plugin's hooks.json names it",
              "multiple": false,
              "name": "NAME",
              "required": true
            }
          ],
          "commands": [],
          "flags": [
            {
              "global": false,
              "help": "The host event it is registered under; absent counts as enforcing",
              "hidden": false,
              "long": "event",
              "possibleValues": [],
              "required": false,
              "short": null,
              "takesValue": true,
              "valueName": "EVENT"
            },
            {
              "global": false,
              "help": "The calling plugin's root, for the version-skew check",
              "hidden": false,
              "long": "plugin-root",
              "possibleValues": [],
              "required": false,
              "short": null,
              "takesValue": true,
              "valueName": "DIR"
            }
          ],
          "hidden": true,
          "longAbout": null,
          "name": "hook",
          "owner": "rust-quality",
          "path": [
            "rust-quality",
            "hook"
          ],
          "placeholder": false
        }
      ],
      "flags": [],
      "hidden": false,
      "longAbout": "rust-quality's rules run after every edit of a .rs file in a Cargo project with cargo on PATH. Violations (oversized files, functions and impl blocks, inline test modules, misplaced tests, lint suppression, unsafe code, unwrap/expect/panic in src, mocks) fail the file's quality-gate entry until it is fixed; missing or verbose docs are advisories.\n\nLimits come from lang.rust in toolu.config.json (maxFileLines, maxFnLines, maxImplLines, noMocks); crates allowed to use unsafe are listed in settings/rust-unsafe-exemptions.txt. toolu rust-quality check runs the same blocking rules over a whole repository. Run toolu doctor to see whether the rule is registered and compiled in.",
      "name": "rust-quality",
      "owner": "rust-quality",
      "path": [
        "rust-quality"
      ],
      "placeholder": false
    },
